The bug was caused by the `nanowait()` function using an integer to represent the timeout in nanoseconds, which led to potential inaccuracies and limitations in specifying wait times. The previous implementation did not allow for precise control over the timeout duration, especially when dealing with different time units. The change to using `struct timespec` allows for more accurate and flexible timeout specifications, addressing the issues that arose from the previous implementation.

